<!--
  Published ACN values for the legacy ACN/PCN method.

  GENERATED FROM ACN.xlsx - do not hand-edit; regenerate if the workbook changes.

  These are NOT computed. There is no callable FAA library for the legacy method
  (ICAO-ACN 1.0 ships a GUI program only, no API, no source - see
  vendor/faa-acn/README.txt), so the values are taken as published and
  interpolated by weight, which is the ICAO convention: ACN is published at the
  maximum and empty weights precisely because it varies essentially linearly
  between them.

  Weights are the workbook's column F, in kilograms. They agree with the maximum
  weights the ACR half reads from the FAA aircraft library to within one pound on
  all four aircraft, so both halves of the window are on the same basis.

  Tyre pressures are not in the workbook; they come from the FAA aircraft library
  (aircraft.xml, Cp/us) - worth confirming against the same source as the ACN
  tables.

  Subgrade letters here are the ACN ones - flexible CBR 15/10/6/3 and rigid
  k 150/80/40/20 MN/m3 - not the ACR ones. Do not mix the two.
-->
<AcnData source="ACN.xlsx (tables constructeur fournies par le dispatch ASL), colonne F en kg">

